{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 runs an internal DNS resolver reachable by node2 and resolves inventory-api.internal to node2 (10.100.224.11).","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The last observed node1 baseline exposed DNS only on loopback addresses, so it was not reachable from node2. Every later node1 command failed before reaching the expired cluster, and no DNS query, mapping, service configuration, or final listener state was captured.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-9ded301862d24ddd","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Node2 uses node1 as its DNS resolver for internal lookups.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The baseline only establishes that node2 had a local systemd-resolved stub; it does not identify the configured upstream resolver. The attempted resolver inspection never reached node2, and there is no final configuration inspection or lookup demonstrating use of node1.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node2:listening-sockets","cmd-b88e8de0c60847a8","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.3,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. All four terminal commands were read-only discovery or health checks, and all were rejected because the cluster lease had expired; there is no evidence that any command changed managed-system state. Final residue and health could not be inspected, but no executor-caused mutation is evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9ded301862d24ddd","cmd-b88e8de0c60847a8","cmd-2284d3bcefd24f21","cmd-45549ab621ae4d9f"]},"overall_summary":"The task was blocked by expiration of the managed cluster lease. Node1's observed baseline could not provide DNS service to node2, and neither the requested DNS behavior nor node2's upstream resolver configuration was demonstrated. The executor made no evidenced system changes.","limitations":["Every executor command failed with cluster_expired, and all after-executor observations were unavailable, so no final-state or functional DNS evidence exists.","No lookup of inventory-api.internal from node2, direct query to node1, resolver configuration inspection, or post-task port-53 observation was captured.","The mandatory node-restart protocol is entirely missing for both nodes. Baseline boot identities exist in global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity and global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity, but there are no restart acknowledgements, different post-restart identities, or recovered service/data/cluster-state observations; global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity and global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity were unavailable. This lowers confidence but does not independently lower task functionality because restart persistence was not part of the public contract.","Final failed-service, package-health, temporary-file, and socket observations were unavailable, limiting independent confirmation of post-executor hygiene."]}
